sara (support): Hey team, Acme reported a failure hitting our /v1/chat with function-calling. They say the model picks the right tool but the call fails schema validation on our side. stack: customer sees 400 schema error.

mike (eng): Can you paste the exact request + response? need the model output and our validation error.

sara (support): Pasting redacted request/response from customer (they repro locally):

```json
// client request to Redwood API (trimmed)
{
  \"model\": \"gpt-open-compat\",
  \"input\": [{
    \"role\": \"user\",
    \"content\": \"Create a new project called Q3-launch\"
  }],
  \"functions\": [{
    \"name\": \"project_create\",
    \"parameters\": {
      \"type\": \"object\",
      \"properties\": {
        \"projectName\": {
          \"type\": \"string\"
        },
        \"visibility\": {
          \"type\": \"string\",
          \"enum\": [\"public\", \"private\"]
        }
      },
      \"required\": [\"projectName\"]
    }
  }]
}
```

sara (support): Model response (as returned by Redwood):

```json
{
  \"tool_call\": {
    \"name\": \"project_create\",
    \"arguments\": \"{\\\"project_name\\\":\\\"Q3-launch\\\",\\\"visibility\\\":\\\"Public\\\"}\"
  }
}
```

sara (support): Our validator throws: `400 schema validation failed: unexpected property 'project_name'` and `invalid enum value 'Public' for visibility`. customer says the call used OpenAI-style keys (snake_case + capitalized enum) while our schema expects camelCase + lowercase enum.

mike (eng): hmm this is classic OpenAI toolcall compatibility mismatch — snake_case vs camelCase and enum casing. They stringified the JSON in arguments (args as a string) too. Are we normally tolerant of stringified args?

anna (infra): Our current OpenAPI/schema layer expects the arguments to be an object not a JSON-string. We do have a compatibility adapter for some older clients but it only handles simple cases. It doesn't normalize keys or enum casing.

tyler (pm): Priority? customer is blocked in prod. They reported 50% of calls failing when the model chooses project_create.

sara (support): Marking P1 for support and sales escalation. Request from customer: short-term workaround + long-term fix.

mike (eng): Short term: we can add a compatibility shim in the request pipeline that, when `tool_call.arguments` is a string, attempts JSON.parse and then normalizes keys and enums. I'll sketch heuristics: convert snake_case -> camelCase, and lowercase enums. But we must avoid silently changing ints/bools and not change content inside free-form strings.

mike (eng): Example mapping code I tried locally (pseudo):

```js
function normalizeArgs(obj) {
  if (typeof obj === 'string') obj = JSON.parse(obj);
  const out = {};
  for (const k of Object.keys(obj)) {
    const camel = k.replace(/_([a-z])/g, (m,p)=>p.toUpperCase());
    let v = obj[k];
    if (typeof v === 'string' && /^[A-Za-z]+$/.test(v)) v = v.toLowerCase(); // enum heuristic
    out[camel] = v;
  }
  return out;
}
```

mike (eng): I can land a fast patch behind a feature flag today to accept stringified args and do snake->camel + enum lowercasing. Need an infra owner to roll safe.

anna (infra): I can handle rollout. We'll gate by header `X-compat-mode: openai-toolcall` so only customers who opt in get transformed. We'll also log a transformation count.

tyler (pm): For long-term, we should document that OpenAI-style tool calling may use different key names and casing. Also discuss whether our model routing should normalize outputs before handing to validation.

sara (support): Customer is ok with an opt-in header for now. They asked if we can automatically enable for customers on older SDKs — they are on SDK v0.9.2.

mike (eng): We can conditionally enable if user-agent or API key metadata indicates SDK v0.9.x. But prefer explicit header.

sara (support): Also note another edge: the model sometimes returns `tool_call.arguments` with extra escaping (double-stringified). Example: `"{\\\"project_name\\\":...}"` — our parser needs to try JSON.parse up to 2x safely.

mike (eng): Good call. I'll implement safe iterative parse with max depth 2 and not throw on parse error — fall back to original string and return validation error so customer sees problem.

anna (infra): Rolling the feature-flagged patch to canary in us-west-2 now. deploy-bot: starting canary deploy...

deploy-bot: canary deploy started for compat-normalizer feature-flag (canary: infra-canary-3) :rocket:

sara (support): Will let customer know and request they add the header while we monitor. Any follow-up actions?

mike (eng): Create a small integration test in our evals harness: feed OpenAI-style toolcall examples (snake_case keys, TitleCase enums, stringified args) and assert we normalize to the function schema. Also add a regression alert if transformation rate spikes unexpectedly.

tyler (pm): Add docs note in Tool Calling compatibility section + SDK guidance. I'll own the doc.

sara (support): Thanks — updating ticket and telling Acme to add header. will follow up if they still see failures. :thumbsup:

mike (eng): postmortem-ish note: we should clarify our public contract for `tool_call.arguments` (object vs string) in the API spec; accept both but prefer object. Will open a JIRA.

